# secretarIA-frontend — public build-time configuration.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file documents the two variables the app reads; it is NOT how
# they get set in production. Because the app is a Next.js STATIC EXPORT served by
# nginx, NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are baked into the bundle at `npm run build` time by
# the ARG/ENV pairs in the Dockerfile. Setting them only in EasyPanel's Environment
# panel has no effect on the built assets.
#
# Local development: copy to `.env.local` and adjust.

# brain-api base — identity, billing and signup live here.
#
# In PRODUCTION this is a same-origin PATH, not an origin: nginx.conf proxies
# `location /api/` to the real brain-api, so the browser only ever talks to one
# origin and the session's refresh token can be a first-party HttpOnly cookie
# (`__Host-refresh_token`). Point it back at the brain-api origin and that cookie
# becomes third-party again — Safari's ITP and Firefox's ETP are then free to drop
# it, and the silent refresh fails for a slice of real users with nothing failing
# loudly. The production value lives in the Dockerfile ARG, as always.
#
# For LOCAL development against a brain-api on another port, put the full origin
# here (scheme + host, no trailing slash). localhost counts as the same SITE
# across ports, so the cookie still works — and brain-api must list this app's
# origin in CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MANAGE_API_BASE_URL=/api
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MANAGE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# secretarIA hub base origin — agenda and clinic configuration live here.
# Must be the service's PUBLIC origin (the browser calls it directly), not
# brain-api's internal SECRETARIA_BASE_URL. Scheme + host only, no trailing slash.
# Leave empty to force the honest "not configured" banner and demo data.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SECRETARIA_HUB_BASE_URL=https://secretaria-secretaria-api.cpux9k.easypanel.host
